$\mathsf{A g@Z n C o/N C F}$ nanohybrids possess outstanding electrocatalytic performance on overall water splitting, mainly because: (1) Ag NWs as templates can improve the conductivity of the catalysts; (2) ZnCo/NCF possesses rich and available electrochemical active sites; (3) the synergistic effect between ZnCo/NCF and Ag NWs contributes to the enhancement of electrocatalytic performance. Those factors synergistically enhance electrocatalytic performance of Ag@ZnCo/NCF nanohybrids toward HER and OER in alkaline solution.
