## 4. Conclusions
We successfully synthesized Ag@ZnCo/NCF nanohybrids by pyrolyzing AgNW@ZIF-8@ZIF-67 precursors. The obtained nanohybrids possess Ag NWs with excellent conductivity and $Z_{\mathrm{{nCo}/N C F}}$ with rich active sites, which cooperate synergistically and enhance electrocatalytic performance on overall water splitting. Compared to other catalysts, the $\mathsf{A g@Z n C o/N C F}$ nanohybrids exhibited lower overpotentials toward HER ( $139\mathrm{mV},$ and OER $(279\mathrm{mV})$ at the current density of $10\mathrm{\mA}$ $\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ in alkaline solution. Meanwhile, $\mathsf{A g@Z n C o/N C F–600}$ nanohybrids possess superior electrochemical stability. We consider that the prominent electrocatalytic performance of Ag@ZnCo/NCF-600 nanohybrids roots in their large specific surface area, excellent structural stability and multicomponent synergistic effect. This work provides a new perspective for the design of electrocatalysts with high catalytic activity and stability, which will be further studied in the future.
